Algorithmic References

The algorithms implemented here are described in published literature. These are
citations, not vendored code — no source from any of the projects below is
included in this repository.

- CROSS: an RNS-BFV / homomorphic encryption accelerator design.
  Parameter sets referred to as "Set B" follow this work.
  https://github.com/EfficientPPML/CROSS

- Langowski and Devadas, on CRNS base conversion.
  IACR ePrint 2025/1068 — https://eprint.iacr.org/2025/1068

- Chen and Ren, OnionPIR v2.
  IACR ePrint 2025/1142 — https://eprint.iacr.org/2025/1142
  Reference implementation: https://github.com/chenyue42/OnionPIRv2

  No source code from the reference implementation is included in this
  repository. Parameter values and configuration names used in docs/pir/, and
  in comments in reference/pir/ and kernels/, were taken from its
  src/includes/database_constants.h (configurations CONFIG_N2048_K1 and
  CONFIG_N2048_K1_COMP) so that results could be compared on the same
  parameter set. The reference implementation, and the repositories it is
  forked from, carry no license. A license was requested from the authors on
  24 September 2026 (https://github.com/nyoos/OnionPIR/issues/1). None had
  been granted at the time of publication.

- Lattigo, a lattice-based homomorphic encryption library, consulted as an
  implementation reference for RNS-BFV.
  https://github.com/tuneinsight/lattigo

- jaxite, Google's JAX library for homomorphic encryption on TPUs. Its CRNS
  base conversion (jaxite_ec/finite_field_context.py) was consulted as an
  implementation reference for reference/he/bfv_bconv_crns.py and
  docs/ir/crns_bconv_lowering.md.
  Licensed under Apache 2.0
  https://github.com/google/jaxite
